# Line endings are content in this repository.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That changes the bytes of every tracked text file, and several of
# them are hashed: dvc.lock and the config files end up in lineage records, so
# the same commit would produce a different hash on Windows than on Linux and
# the traceability claim would quietly stop holding.
#
# Normalise to LF everywhere. Every tracked file here is text, so one rule is
# enough; add explicit `binary` lines if that ever stops being true.
* text=auto eol=lf
